            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "just my personal opinion.\n\novercomplicating the issue.\nWe do not have so many update daemons to justify this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "fwiw, I did it partially because there were multiple mistakes in dependencies and subdirectories needed by different daemons, because the previous code had way too many if-blocks.  This makes it clear 'option X needs libraries A, B and subdirectories 1 and 2', rather than the hope that someone keeps the logic all right."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You see there are 3 commits earlier in the chain \"meson: fix ...\".  These were all mistakes in the if-logic and/or subdirectory cross-dependencies."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> because the previous code had way too many if-blocks\n\nAnd the proposed code has `if` and `for` blocks nested 4 levels deep.\n\n> These were all mistakes in the if-logic and/or subdirectory cross-dependencies.\n\nThe existing logic is easy to understand. If you need some subdir or dependency,\n`or` the meson option to the corresponding `if` statement.\n\n\nIf we need to make sure the dependencies and subdirs are correctly defined for\nall permutations of the meson options, i see no other way than to compile all those permutations in CI.\n\nLooks like that is supported by jenkins\n\nhttps://www.jenkins.io/blog/2019/11/22/welcome-to-the-matrix/"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> And the proposed code has if and for blocks nested 4 levels deep.\n\nI don\u2019t see how that is equivalent. The previous code had options reused adhoc in different of blocks. It was not clear where each option was used.\n\n> The existing logic is easy to understand. If you need some subdir or dependency,\nor the meson option to the corresponding if statement.\n\nMaybe it was \u201ceasy to understand\u201d but it was clearly not \u201ceasy to get right\u201d.  And if it was so \u201ceasy to understand\u201d wouldn\u2019t the reviewers (and the authors) have noticed that it was wrong?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Maybe it was \u201ceasy to understand\u201d but it was clearly not \u201ceasy to get right\u201d. And if it was so \u201ceasy to understand\u201d wouldn\u2019t the reviewers (and the authors) have noticed that it was wrong?\n\nPeople usually just try things until it compiles for them.\nPeople do not usually try multiple permutations of meson options (especially non-default configurations)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 93,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@alexander.hansen@9elements.com The only reason these for-loops exist are because meson unfortunately does not allow sets to be mutable.  If it did, or were enhanced to allow it to be in the future, these collapse to a set-append."
                }
            ],
